{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Sash_Whip","to":"Sash Whip"},{"from":"Fame_and_Fortune","to":"Fame and Fortune"},{"from":"Twin_Strike","to":"Twin Strike"},{"from":"Beam_Cell","to":"Beam Cell"},{"from":"Foreign_Influence","to":"Foreign Influence"}],"pages":{"2060":{"pageid":2060,"ns":0,"title":"Beam Cell","revisions":[{"revid":56895,"parentid":55641,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Beam Cell\n|Image       = Blue-BeamCell.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (3;4) damage.<br>Apply (1;2) {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Vulnerable\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}}\n{{C|Beam Cell}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1843":{"pageid":1843,"ns":0,"title":"Burst","revisions":[{"revid":55676,"parentid":50531,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Burst\n|Image       = Green-Burst.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = This turn, your next (Skill is;2 Skills are) played twice.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Burst}}{{C|Burst}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Burst}}, which will make the following {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card(s) this turn play twice, for the first amount of cards equal to the amount of {{BD|Burst}}. \n\nHaving more than 1 {{BD|Burst}} will not increase the amount of times a single {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card is duplicated, but increases the amount of cards that can be duplicated when played.\n\nThe second play of these cards counts as a separate card being played, but this card is not added to your draw or discard pile, and is not {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} unless the card would {{KW|Exhaust}} upon being played normally. \n\nThe second play of these cards does not expend any {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy'''. The second play of an X-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card will use the same value of X as the first.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The second play of a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card only starts after the first play is fully resolved. In effect, it is as if the two cards were played with a pause in between, resulting in interactions including but not limited to:\n** The second play of {{C|Catalyst}} will multiply the {{BD|Poison}} that was already multiplied by the first play, effectively squaring the effect of the card.\n** The second play of {{C|Calculated Gamble}} or {{C|Storm of Steel}} will [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] the cards that were respectively drawn or generated by the first play.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Burst}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}, it can duplicate itself, resulting in more {{BD|Burst}}, which means more {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} being duplicated.\n** For example, if the player has no {{BD|Burst}} and plays {{C|Burst}}, {{C|Burst}}, {{C|Bouncing Flask}} and {{C|Catalyst}}, in that order, the order of operations will be:\n# The first {{C|Burst}} provides the player with the {{BD|Burst}} effect. \n# The second {{C|Burst}} is now played twice, consuming the initial {{BD|Burst}} but then providing 2 additional stacks of it. \n# {{C|Bouncing Flask}} is then played twice and one {{BD|Burst}} will be consumed.\n# {{C|Catalyst}} is then played twice and the last {{BD|Burst}} will be consumed.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The second play of a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card counts as the play of a wholly separate card. All consequences of playing that card will still apply:\n** The effects of the card itself.\n** Anything that triggers or increments upon playing a ({{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}) card, including but not limited to: \n*** Effects such as {{BD|After Image}} and {{BD|Thousand Cuts}}.\n*** Relics such as {{R|Letter Opener}} and {{R|Ink Bottle}}.\n*** Card limits such as {{R|Velvet Choker}} and the Time Eater's {{BD|Time Warp}}.\n\n* Using {{BD|Burst}} on {{C|Blade Dance}} creates 6 (8 if {{C|Blade Dance}} is upgraded) {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} in hand, which can significantly advance counters on relics such as {{R|Shuriken}} and {{R|Nunchaku}} when played, but potentially exceeds the hand size limit in which case the remaining {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} will be added to the discard pile.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies === \n* Since {{C|Panic Button}} immediately applies the {{BD|No Block}} debuff, using {{BD|Burst}} on {{C|Panic Button}} provides no extra {{KW|Block}}. \n* Since the first play of {{C|Expertise}} will fill the hand to the specified amount of cards, the second play will have no effect.\n\n== Bugs ==\n=== Bursting a Burst ===\nOn the Mobile version, there is a bug that can occur when Bursting a Burst. If you have exactly 1 stack of Burst, and you play Burst, then what happens is:\n* The first play of Burst will occur, adding 1 (2) stacks.\n* The game attempts to remove the stack of Burst that has been consumed. Due to a bug, it then removes '''all stacks of Burst, including the one(s) just added'''.\n* The second play will happen, adding 1 (2) stacks.\nInstead of ending up with 2 (4) stacks afterwards as expected, you will only have 1 (2), the same as if you hadn't Burst it at all.\n\nIf you have 2 or more stacks of Burst and play Burst, the game handles the interaction properly.\n\n== Trivia ==\n\n* Along with {{C|Double Tap}} and {{C|Amplify}}, one of the three 'play a card twice' Skills in the game.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1834":{"pageid":1834,"ns":0,"title":"Clothesline","revisions":[{"revid":56386,"parentid":55699,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Clothesline\n| Image       = Red-Clothesline.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal (12;14) damage.<br>Apply (2;3) {{BD|Weak}}.\n| GivesToEnemy = Weak\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Weak}}{{C|Clothesline}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 12 (14 if upgraded) damage and applies 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1914":{"pageid":1914,"ns":0,"title":"Combust","revisions":[{"revid":55704,"parentid":50415,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Rename|Combust|Inferno}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Combust\n|Image       = Red-Combust.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = At the end of your turn, lose 1 HP and deal (5;7) damage to ALL enemies.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Combust}}{{C|Combust}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 5 (7 if upgraded) {{BD|Combust}}, which deals that amount of damage to '''ALL''' enemies and costs you 1 HP every at the end of your turn.\n\nPlaying {{C|Combust}} multiple times will increase the amount of {{BD|Combust}} and will increase the HP loss of the entire stack of {{BD|Combust}} by 1, for every copy played.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Tungsten Rod}} completely negates the damage from the first play of {{C|Combust}}.\n* {{C|Combust}} can be used to reliably and repeatedly trigger {{C|Rupture}} and {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}, and lower the cost of {{C|Blood for Blood}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Since {{BD|Combust}} activates after you end your turn but before you discard your hand, any draw as a result of {{BD|Combust}}'s HP loss in combination with {{R|Runic Cube}} or {{R|Centennial Puzzle}} will be wasted.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 20: Immolate'''\n** Combust+ card damage buff. 6 -> 7.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 19: Seed'''\n** Combust card buff. Damage 4 -> 5.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2132":{"pageid":2132,"ns":0,"title":"FTL","revisions":[{"revid":50588,"parentid":36242,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = FTL\n|Image       = Blue-FTL.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (5;6) damage. If you have played less than (3;4) cards this turn, draw 1 card.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|FTL}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 5 (6 if upgraded) damage, and if a maximum of 3 (4 if upgraded) cards were played before this one, it will draw 1 card as well, meaning it functionally replaces itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Combines very well with {{C|All for One}}, as {{C|FTL}} can give a positive amount of draw this way. \n* As it is 0-cost, {{C|FTL}} can be drawn without being discarded by {{C|Scrape}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2377":{"pageid":2377,"ns":0,"title":"Fame and Fortune","revisions":[{"revid":53300,"parentid":50768,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"#REDIRECT [[Wish#Fame and Fortune]]"}}}]},"2280":{"pageid":2280,"ns":0,"title":"Fasting","revisions":[{"revid":55771,"parentid":50661,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Fasting\n|Image       = Purple-Fasting.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Gain (3;4) {{BD|Strength}}. <br>Gain (3;4) {{BD|Dexterity}}. <br>Gain 1 less {{Icon|PE}} at the start of each turn.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Fasting}}{{C|Fasting}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded) of both {{BD|Strength}} and {{BD|Dexterity}}. It also gives one {{BD|Fasting}}, which gives you less energy at the start of every turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Deva Form}} will quickly make the downside of this card irrelevant.\n** Be careful about the order in which these are played, as playing {{C|Fasting}} first will make it harder to play {{C|Deva Form}}.\n\n* {{R|Orange Pellets}} can remove the {{BD|Fasting}} you get from this card.\n* Sources of {{BD|Artifact}}, such as {{R|Clockwork Souvenir}}, {{P|Ancient Potion}}, {{C|Core Surge}} and {{C|Panacea}} can prevent this card from applying {{BD|Fasting}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2052":{"pageid":2052,"ns":0,"title":"Flechettes","revisions":[{"revid":55782,"parentid":50511,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Flechettes\n|Image       = Green-Flechettes.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (4;6) damage for each Skill in your hand.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Flechettes}} is a 1{{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card for the [[Silent]]. It deals 4 (6 if upgraded) damage, for an amount of times equal to the amount of {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} cards in your hand. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits once from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}} per hit, so for every {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card in hand.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many'''\n** Fixed rare Flechette card VFX crash.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2287":{"pageid":2287,"ns":0,"title":"Foreign Influence","revisions":[{"revid":54859,"parentid":50663,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Foreign Influence\n|Image       = Purple-ForeignInfluence.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Choose 1 of 3 Attacks of any color to add to your hand.( ;<br>It costs 0 this turn.)<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Foreign Influence}} is a 0 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. \n\nIt will generate 3 {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards, out of which you can choose up to one to add to your hand, after which this {{C|Foreign Influence}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. If upgraded, the chosen {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} will have its normal cost replaced by 0, but X cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards generated this way will still consume all your energy. \n\n{{C|Foreign Influence}} can only generate cards you can find in card rewards through character choice or custom run modifiers, and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source:\n** {{C|Feed}}\n** {{C|Reaper}}\n** {{C|Lesson Learned}}\n** {{C|Bite}}\n** {{C|Ritual Dagger}}\n** {{C|Shiv}}\n** {{C|Smite}}\n** {{C|Through Violence}}\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2292":{"pageid":2292,"ns":0,"title":"Halt","revisions":[{"revid":55811,"parentid":55438,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Halt\n|Image       = Purple-Halt.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Gain (3;4) {{KW|Block}}. <br>If you are in {{KW|Wrath}}, gain (9;14) additional {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Wrath}}\n{{C|Halt}} is a 0 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, and an additional 9 (14 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} if you are in the {{KW|Wrath}} {{KW|Stance}} when playing it.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits two times from {{BD|Dexterity}} while in {{KW|Wrath}}.\n** Notably synergizes with {{C|Fasting}} as {{C|Halt}} costs 0.\n** Notably synergizes with {{R|Duality}} as it allows you to rack up large sums of temporary {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n\n* Depends on being in {{KW|Wrath}} for its full effect, meaning it synergizes with ways to enter that {{KW|Stance}}:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Eruption}} and {{C|Tantrum}} can reliably make you enter {{KW|Wrath}}.\n* {{C|Crescendo}} can make you enter {{KW|Wrath}} once at any point after first drawing it, making it a good fallback.\n* {{C|Indignation}} synergizes well, as it allows you to enter {{KW|Wrath}} and still receive full benefits from itself while remaining in {{KW|Wrath}}.\n* {{C|Simmering Fury}}, although it will only make you enter {{KW|Wrath}} the next turn. \n\n==== b) Potions ====\n* {{P|Stance Potion}} allows you to pick between entering {{KW|Calm}} and {{KW|Wrath}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1925":{"pageid":1925,"ns":0,"title":"Inflame","revisions":[{"revid":56752,"parentid":55824,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Inflame\n| Image       = Red-Inflame.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (2;3) {{BD|Strength}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Strength\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Strength}}\n{{C|Inflame}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Strength}}.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2457":{"pageid":2457,"ns":0,"title":"Insight","revisions":[{"revid":50758,"parentid":36957,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Insight\n|Image       = Colorless-Insight.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}. <br>Draw (2;3) cards. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Insight}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 2 (3 if upgraded) cards and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n== Creating Insight ==\n{{C|Insight}} can only be created in combat by, playing {{C|Evaluate}}, {{C|Pray}} or {{C|Study}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Starting when you have {{C|Master Reality}} in play, {{C|Evaluate}}, {{C|Pray}} and {{C|Study}} will create upgraded {{C|Insight|Insights}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2117":{"pageid":2117,"ns":0,"title":"Loop","revisions":[{"revid":55843,"parentid":50596,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Loop\n|Image       = Blue-Loop.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = At the start of your turn, trigger the passive ability of your next Orb (1 time;2 times).\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Loop}}\n{{C|Loop}} is an 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. <!--At the start of your turn, the right-most {{KW|Orbs|Orb}} has its {{KW|Passive}} triggered 1 (2) additional times.-->\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* While all of the Orb types benefit from Loop, {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} particularly benefit from the additional [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]], allowing them to grow quickly: {{C|Darkness}}, {{C|Doom and Gloom}}, {{C|Chaos}}, {{C|Rainbow}}, {{R|Symbiotic Virus}}, {{P|Essence of Darkness}}\n* {{BD|Focus}} makes the [[Orbs#Passive|Passive]] effects of non-{{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} much better: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* In addition to general Orb sources, cards that can manually {{KW|Evoke}} the first Orb can be very useful for setting up Loop on the correct Orb: {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, {{C|Multi-Cast}}\n** {{C|Fission}} may be used in a similar fashion, but requires {{KW|Channel|Channeling}} the Orb you want afterwards.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The additional '''Passives''' of Loop stack with the added Passives from {{R|Emotion Chip}}, as well as those of {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}}, if the Orb in question is a {{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orb}}.\n* If you have no {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orbs at the start of your turn, Loop will not do anything.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2452":{"pageid":2452,"ns":0,"title":"Miracle","revisions":[{"revid":55465,"parentid":53387,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Miracle\n|Image       = Colorless-Miracle.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}. <br>Gain ({{Icon|PE}};{{Icon|PE}} {{Icon|PE}}). <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Energy\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}} {{Keyword Infobox|Energy}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}} \n{{C|Miracle}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n== Creating Miracle ==\n{{C|Miracle}} can only be created in combat:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Collect}} will add a certain number of upgraded {{C|Miracle|Miracles}} to your hand over the span of the same amount of turns.\n* {{C|Deus Ex Machina}} will add 2 (3 if upgraded) {{C|Miracle|Miracles}} to your hand when drawn.\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Pure Water}} will add 1 {{C|Miracle}} to your hand at the start of combat.\n* {{R|Holy Water}}, which replaces {{R|Pure Water}} will add 3 {{C|Miracle|Miracles}} to your hand at the start of combat. \n==== Potions ====\n* {{P|Bottled Miracle}} will add 2 {{C|Miracle|Miracles}} to your hand.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Starting when you have {{C|Master Reality}} in play, {{C|Collect}}, {{C|Deus Ex Machina}} and {{P|Bottled Miracle}} will create upgraded {{C|Miracle|Miracles}}.\n* As a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} that {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Miracle}} can be used to easily activate the extra effects of {{C|Crush Joints}} or {{C|Sanctity}}.\n* {{R|Ice Cream}} gives more freedom in deciding when to play {{C|Miracle}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2415":{"pageid":2415,"ns":0,"title":"Ragnarok","revisions":[{"revid":55912,"parentid":50707,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Ragnarok\n|Image       = Purple-Ragnarok.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|Description = Deal (5;6) damage to a random enemy (5;6) times.\n}}\n{{C|Ragnarok}} is a 3 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 5 (6 if upgraded) damage 5 (6 if upgraded) times.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* * Benefits five (six if upgraded) times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2282":{"pageid":2282,"ns":0,"title":"Sash Whip","revisions":[{"revid":55931,"parentid":54831,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Sash Whip\n|Image       = Purple-SashWhip.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (8;10) damage.<br>If the last card played this combat was an Attack, apply (1;2) {{BD|Weak}}.\n}}\n{{C|Sash Whip}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 8 (10 if upgraded) damage. If the last card played this combat was an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}, this card also applies 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2416":{"pageid":2416,"ns":0,"title":"Scrawl","revisions":[{"revid":54001,"parentid":50708,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Scrawl\n|Image       = Purple-Scrawl.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = Draw cards until your hand is full. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Scrawl}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws cards until your hand is full, and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The {{C|Scrawl}} that was played does not count towards the amount of cards in hand for the purpose of its own effect.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The beta art of Scrawl is a reference to the SpongeBob Squarepants \"What I learned in boating school\" meme.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]] [[Category:ToUpdate]]"}}}]},"2099":{"pageid":2099,"ns":0,"title":"Storm","revisions":[{"revid":55959,"parentid":50609,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Storm\n|Image       = Blue-Storm.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}. <br>)Whenever you play a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card, {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Lightning}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Storm}}{{C|Storm}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}. <!---Once played, it will {{KW|Channel}} a {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} every time a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} is played. When upgraded, it becomes {{KW|Innate}}.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The Orb is not {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} by Storm until ''after'' the {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} has resolved.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Mummified Hand}} reduces the cost of a random non-0 cost, non-{{KW|Unplayable}} card in your hand cost 0 this turn, allowing {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} to be played more easily.\n* {{R|Bird-Faced Urn}} heals you for 2 HP every time a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} is played.\n* {{C|Heatsinks}} draws 1 (2) card(s) for each {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} played.\n\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Darkness}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} more frequently.\n* {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits more times for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat, and {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hit all enemies.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Playing Storm does not {{KW|Channel}} an Orb, only subsequent Powers do.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Lightning}} Orbs less effective.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Fixed typos on Storm Power's description.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1837":{"pageid":1837,"ns":0,"title":"Twin Strike","revisions":[{"revid":55988,"parentid":50406,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Twin Strike\n|Image       = Red-TwinStrike.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (5;7) damage twice.\n}}\n{{C|Twin Strike}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 5 (7 if upgraded) damage twice. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits 2 times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n* {{C|Twin Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 for both hits from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1455":{"pageid":1455,"ns":0,"title":"Zap","revisions":[{"revid":56336,"parentid":56010,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Zap\n| Image       = Blue-Zap.png\n| Color       = Blue\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Lightning}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Channel, Lightning\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Channel}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Lightning}}\n{{C|Zap}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.<!---It {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 1 {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} when played.--->\n\n== Obtaining Zap ==\nThe [[Defect]] starts the game with one copy of Zap in their deck.\n\nZap cannot be obtained through regular card rewards, but can be obtained in the {{E|Match and Keep}} Event. \n\nIf you already have Zap in your deck, it can be duplicated using {{R|Dolly's Mirror}} or the {{E|Duplicator}} Event.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Darkness}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} more frequently.\n* {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits more times for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat, and {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hit all enemies.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Lightning}} Orbs less effective.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}